      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Is it possible to add SendCustomEvent and SendCustomEventDelayed with parameters to the official SDK? I am very grateful that Genesis implemented one, but I also hope the development team could consider including those functions in official SDK for better compatibility with future SDK releases.\n\nThe reason I want these functions is that although the newly released networked version covers many use cases, it does not allow non-syncable arguments, like object references. I am trying to make an event system where event calls are broadcasted to multiple receivers that come in different classes, and I want to pass object references to them as event context.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-12-16T17:48:30.623Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If I want to pass a parameter to custom event receiver, even now, I could it by using public program variable and executing SetProgramVariable before SendCustomEvent. Comparing that, for example, OnCollisionEnter event uses implicitly defined variable \"onCollisionEnterOther\".\n\nI think it will be useful and user friendly if parameter passing can be written directly in sender side SendCustomEvent node and receiver side CustomEvent node as a kind of syntax sugar.",
  "error": null,
